**capitalize(word)**

Write `capitalize(word)`: first letter upper-case, the rest lower-case. `""` stays `""`.

```js
function capitalize(word) {
  // TODO
  return word;
}
```

notes.back:
// Why: `word[0]` is undefined for "", and calling a method on undefined throws. `slice(1)`
// returns everything after the first character.
// Docs: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/String/slice
function capitalize(word) {
  if (word === "") return "";
  return word[0].toUpperCase() + word.slice(1).toLowerCase();
}

