**isPalindrome(text)**

Write `isPalindrome(text)`: true if `text` reads the same backwards, ignoring case, spaces and punctuation.

```js
function isPalindrome(text) {
  // TODO
  return false;
}
```

notes.back:
// Why: Clean the text first, then compare it with its reverse. Strings have no reverse():
// spread into an array, reverse, and join back.
// Docs: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Array/reverse
function isPalindrome(text) {
  const letters = text.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9]/g, "");
  return letters === [...letters].reverse().join("");
}

